    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AE469E23D63EE01425E773C19A546C6B/jobs/584580": {
      "title": "Health Educator/Clinical Counselor",
      "description": "Health Educator/Clinical Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Health Educator/Clinical Counselor Lasell University - Newton, MA 02466 Apply Overview Salary Range $60,000.00 - $70,000.00 Salary Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description JOB DESCRIPTION Job Title:   Health Educator/Clinical Counselor Division:     Academic and Student Affairs                   Department:  Counseling Center Reports to:  Director of the Counseling Center Employment Status: Full Time Part Time   Calendar Year   Academic Year   9 months 10 months JOB SUMMARY: The Health Educator/Clinical Counselor is one of the professional staff members who compose the staff of the Counseling Center. Reporting to the Director of the Counseling Center, the position of Health Educator/Clinical Counselor has a dual focus:  the coordination and delivery of health/wellness programming; and the provision of direct service mental health counseling to the undergraduate student body. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person or persons assigned to this job.  They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities.  Lasell University has the right to add or change the job responsibilities at any time . Serve as the University’s Health Educator, and in that capacity: coordinate the University’s alcohol education program, including the facilitation of AlcoholEdu, and the creation of activities associated with the annual National Collegiate Alcohol Awareness Week; design and coordinate the Peer Health Education program including the recruitment, selection, training, and supervision of the Peer Health Educators (PHEs); as necessary, supervise undergraduate Lasell student (s) serving as Peer Health Intern(s); collaborate with colleagues across the University community to devise a comprehensive menu of health-related programs, to be presented in campus-wide settings and (on request) in the residential buildings. Provide direct service to members of the Lasell University student body:  conduct drop-in and intake sessions; provide short term counseling; provide case management services for off-campus referrals when long term therapy and/or specialized treatment is required; c oordinate care with collateral off-campus providers and consulting psychiatrist, when deemed necessary; respond to student mental health emergencies; work with Director to coordinate mental health care for students returning to campus after psychiatric hospitalizations; m aintain appropriate client records, including case documentation in confidential files, and scheduling and data collection through Titanium . Provide consultation to Lasell staff and faculty, and families of students, within guidelines of client confidentiality. Promote and provide campus-wide programming on topics including: awareness/prevention of substance abuse and mental illness, sexual assault, and domestic violence; design and implement training/education programs for Residential Life staff, Orientation Leaders, and other student leaders on these (and other) topics. Communication: students and their families; faculty, staff and administration; establish and maintain close working relationships with various Student Affairs functional units, Campus Police, the Advising Office and the Academic Achievement Center. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility: Does this position supervise the equivalent of two (2) or more full-time employees?    Yes No Qualifications MINIMUM KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS REQUIRED BY THE JOB: Minimum Education level: Appropriate master’s degree in counseling related field such as: social work, psychology or counseling, with professional licensure in Commonwealth of Massachusetts (see below). Computer skills: Microsoft Office Other Requirements of the Job: experience in mental health counseling/substance abuse , preferably in a college/university setting; experience in educational programming with adolescents/ young adults; ability to work with a wide range of developmental, mental health and substance abuse issues in older adolescent and young adult population. CERTIFICATION, REGISTRATION OR LICENSURE REQUIRED BY THE JOB: Current professional licensure in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts (LCSW, LICSW, LMHC, or psychology); current professional liability coverage (malpractice insurance); maintenance of up-to-date continuing education requirements. WHY LASELL? Competitive salary Comprehensive benefits package including: Medical Dental Vision Retirement Tuition benefits Generous time off Hybrid/remote work options Lasell University is committed to equal opportunity in every aspect of hiring and employment. Lasell proactively reviews its policies and practices to assure that decisions with respect to every dimension of employment are made without regard to age, color of skin, disability, gender expression and identity, genetic predisposition, marital status, national origin, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran's status, status as a victim of domestic violence, and all other protected groups and classes under Federal and State Laws and executive orders. Share job details to About LASELL UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AE469E23D63EE01425E773C19A546C6B/jobs/584572": {
      "title": "Clinical Counselor",
      "description": "Clinical Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Clinical Counselor Lasell University - Newton, MA 02466 Apply Overview Salary Range $50,000.00 - $60,000.00 Salary Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description JOB DESCRIPTION Job Title:   Clinical Counselor Division:  Academic and Student Affairs                        Department:  Counseling Center Reports to: Counseling Center Director Employment Status: Full Time Part Time   Calendar Year   Academic Year 9 months 10 months JOB SUMMARY: The Clinical Counselor is one of the professional staff members who comprise the staff of the Counseling Center. Reporting to the Director of the Counseling Center, the Clinical Counselor provides direct service mental health counseling to the undergraduate student body, and delivers psycho-educational programming. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person or persons assigned to this job.  They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities.  Lasell University has the right to add or change the job responsibilities at any time . 1. Provide direct service to members of the Lasell College student body:  conduct drop-in and intake sessions; provide short term counseling; provide case management services for off-campus referrals when long term therapy and/or specialized treatment is required; c oordinate care with collateral off-campus providers and consulting psychiatrist, when deemed necessary; respond to student mental health emergencies; work with Director to coordinate mental health care for students returning to campus after psychiatric hospitalizations; m aintain appropriate client records, including case documentation in confidential files, and scheduling and data collection through Titanium . 2.  As necessary, provide intake and counseling sessions for students referred through Lasell’s Conduct system, including students who have been transported to the hospital for alcohol-related issues. 3. Provide consultation to Lasell staff and faculty, and families of students, within guidelines of client confidentiality. 4. Work with colleagues on Counseling Center staff to design and implement campus-wide, psycho-educational outreach programs on relevant developmental topics related to mental health and healthy relationships.  Assist with the training of Resident Assistants, Area Coordinators, Orientation Leaders, Peer Mentors, etc. as required. 5. Communication: students and their families; faculty, staff and administration; establish and maintain close working relationships with colleagues across campus, including (but not limited to):  various Student Affairs functional units, Campus Police, the Advising Office, and the Academic Achievement Center. 6. Other duties as assigned. Tier Structure Subject to the completion of a Remote Work Agreement, this is a Tier 2 – Hybrid/flex position requiring on-campus work while allowing for some remote work as well. Supervisory Responsibility: Does this position supervise the equivalent of two (2) or more full-time employees?    Yes No Qualifications MINIMUM KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS REQUIRED BY THE JOB: Minimum Education level: Appropriate master’s degree in counseling related field such as: social work, psychology or counseling, with professional licensure in Commonwealth of Massachusetts (see below). Computer skills: Microsoft Office Other Requirements of the Job: Experience in mental health counseling , preferably in a college/university setting; ability to work with a wide range of developmental, mental health and substance abuse issues in older adolescent and young adult population. Must have excellent interpersonal skills; comfort and competence developing and delivering presentations; competency in working with students individually and in groups; and demonstrated competency and comfort working in, and with, a diverse community. CERTIFICATION, REGISTRATION OR LICENSURE REQUIRED BY THE JOB: Current professional licensure in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts (LICSW, LMHC, or psychology); current professional liability coverage (malpractice insurance); maintenance of up-to-date continuing education requirements. WHY LASELL? Competitive salary Comprehensive benefits package including: Medical Dental Vision Retirement Tuition benefits Generous time off Hybrid/remote work options Lasell University is committed to equal opportunity in every aspect of hiring and employment. Lasell proactively reviews its policies and practices to assure that decisions with respect to every dimension of employment are made without regard to age, color of skin, disability, gender expression and identity, genetic predisposition, marital status, national origin, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran's status, status as a victim of domestic violence, and all other protected groups and classes under Federal and State Laws and executive orders. Share job details to About LASELL UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AE469E23D63EE01425E773C19A546C6B/jobs/579912": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty-Business Analytics",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty-Business Analytics You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty-Business Analytics Lasell University - Newton, MA 02466 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,350.00 - $3,350.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Graduate Degree Category Faculty Apply Description Adjunct Professor – Undergraduate Business Analytics Institution: Lasell University – Department of Data Science Location: Newton, MA on campus twice a week Employment Type: Adjunct (per semester) Start Date: Fall 2026 (September 8, 2026) This position is approximately 6-8 hours a week This position also does not qualify for any type of employment-sponsorship. Position Overview The Department of Data Science and Business Management seek an enthusiastic adjunct faculty member to teach an undergraduate course that introduces the conceptual and technical foundations of Business Analytics and Big Data. The instructor will guide students through real ‑ world analytics practices, data handling, and the use of industry ‑ standard tools, preparing them for data ‑ driven roles across the business sector. Course Description The course provides the conceptual and technical foundations of various aspects of Data Analytics. The purpose is to prepare students with foundation skills in Big Data, a skill widely needed and valued across the business world. Students will explore the analytical process, how data is created, stored, accessed, and how organizations work with data to create environments where analytics can flourish. Learning Objectives / Outcomes 1. Understand the strategy and technologies of business analytics. 2. Develop foundational skills in Big Data. 3. Describe descriptive, predictive, and prescriptive analytics. 4. Create and interpret data visualizations. 5. Perform data modeling and review data ‑ mining, simulation, and optimization methods. 6. Use business ‑ analytics technologies (Excel, Tableau, SQL, etc.). Key Topics & Skills Students Will Gain - Classification of qualitative vs. quantitative data. - Construction and interpretation of visual data displays. - Calculation and discussion of measures of central tendency. - Evaluation of various analytics types. - Proficiency with Excel, Tableau, and SQL. - Understanding of company operations, profiles, and business dynamics. - Identification of data ‑ driven business opportunities. - Bridging business problems with analytical models. - Communication of technical analysis to both technical and non ‑ technical audiences. - Assessment of financial, operational, and ethical implications of data ‑ driven solutions. - Teach 3 credit hours of the Business Analytics course. - Prepare and deliver lectures, labs, and assignments aligned with the provided syllabus. - Design and grade assessments (quizzes, exams, projects). Qualifications - Required: Master’s degree (or higher) in Business Analytics, Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, or a closely related field. - Demonstrated expertise with analytics tools such as Excel, Tableau, SQL, and familiarity with Python/R a plus. - Prior industry experience in data analytics, consulting, or a related business function. - Prior teaching or tutoring experience at the college level preferred. - Ability to convey complex technical concepts clearly to undergraduate students. Share job details to About LASELL UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AE469E23D63EE01425E773C19A546C6B/jobs/577027": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Economics",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Economics You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Economics Lasell University - Newton, MA 02466 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,350.00 - $3,350.00 Salary Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Category Faculty Apply Description Lasell University | Early College Partnership Location: Private high school in Waltham, MA Course Format: In-person Schedule: Tuesdays & Thursdays, 6:00–7:15 p.m. Total hours of work per week for this position is 150 minutes. This position does not qualify for any type of employment-sponsorship. Position Overview Lasell University is seeking a qualified Adjunct Instructor to teach ECON101: Principles of Economics: Microeconomics as part of the University's Early College partnership with a private high school in Waltham, Massachusetts. The successful candidate will teach a college-level introductory economics course to high school students participating in Lasell's Early College program. This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced college instructor who enjoys working with emerging college students and bringing undergraduate-level business and economics concepts to a high school setting. Course Description ECON101: Principles of Economics: Microeconomics is an introduction to the principles of economic behavior of individuals, firms, and industries in a mixed economic system. Topics include consumer demand; elasticity; supply and costs of production; allocation of economic resources; international trade; and the role of government in promoting economic welfare. Responsibilities The adjunct instructor will: Deliver engaging, college-level instruction in microeconomics. Develop and deliver course materials consistent with Lasell University's course objectives and expectations. Create an engaging learning environment appropriate for high school students earning college credit. Assess student learning through assignments, examinations, projects, and other appropriate measures. Provide timely and substantive feedback to students. Maintain accurate records of student attendance and academic progress. Utilize Lasell University's Canvas learning management system. Communicate regularly with students and the Early College partnership team. Coordinate, as appropriate, with the partnering school's faculty and staff. Qualifications Qualifications Required: Master's degree or higher in Economics, Business, or a closely related field. College-level teaching experience in economics or a related discipline. Preferred: Experience teaching introductory economics or microeconomics. Experience teaching high school, Early College, dual-enrollment, or other pre-college students. Experience with Canvas or another learning management system. Ability to make complex economic concepts accessible and engaging to students with varying levels of academic preparation. Additional Information This is a single-course adjunct teaching opportunity for the Fall semester. The instructor will teach the course in person at a private high school in Waltham, MA, on Tuesdays and Thursdays from 6:00–7:15 p.m. Compensation: $3,350 for the course. Lasell University is committed to equal opportunity in every aspect of hiring and employment. Lasell proactively reviews its policies and practices to assure that decisions with respect to every dimension of employment are made without regard to age, color of skin, disability, gender expression and identity, genetic predisposition, marital status, national origin, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran's status, status as a victim of domestic violence, and all other protected groups and classes under Federal and State Laws and executive orders. Share job details to About LASELL UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/AE469E23D63EE01425E773C19A546C6B/jobs/574036": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Spanish Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Spanish Instructor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Spanish Instructor Lasell University - Newton, MA 02466 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,500.00 - $4,333.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Category Faculty Apply Description Part-time Spanish Language Instructor The World Language Program in the School of Humanities, Education, Justice & Social Sciences at Lasell College is seeking a part-time instructor to teach an Introductory Spanish for Professionals course. We currently have an opening for 1 class session that starts Sept 2. SPAN111 is the first level of Elementary Spanish – we anticipate that the faculty member hired will also teach ASL112 in the spring semester. This is a face-to-face course that has been scheduled Monday/Wednesday 11:00 – 12:14. Responsibilities and Duties: Develop a syllabus and course outline for students that clearly communicates course learning outcomes and focuses on the ability to communicate in Spanish in professional settings for Psychology, Criminal Justice, and Health Professions. Provide instruction for all sessions of assigned courses utilizing the college philosophy of connected learning. Maintain office hours each week. Incorporate Canvas (online learning platform) into the course. Keep accurate records of student progress (grades) and complete mid-semester and final grade reports. Collaborate with other language instructors to determine appropriate leveling and pre-requisite work Qualifications Qualifications: Experience teaching Spanish, as well as a master’s degree or ABD in a related field are required. A willingness to incorporate the college’s Connected Learning Philosophy into the course is also important. Lasell University is committed to equal opportunity in every aspect of hiring and employment. Lasell proactively reviews its policies and practices to assure that decisions with respect to every dimension of employment are made without regard to age, color of skin, disability, gender expression and identity, genetic predisposition, marital status, national origin, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran's status, status as a victim of domestic violence, and all other protected groups and classes under Federal and State Laws and executive orders. Share job details to About LASELL UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
